/* Pass-4 mechanism calibration output (class-3 deferred campaign,
   Task 1; review round 1 added the "atom" atom-top-guard regression
   row and the noise/label notes below).
   Generated: sbcl --tls-limit 100000 --core test/mr_rules.core
     --noinform --very-quiet -b probes/corpus/06-calibration.pass4.mac
   Date: 2026-08-30 (UTC)  Build: Maxima branch_5_50_base_84_g4204fb669 / SBCL 2.6.7
   Core fingerprint at run: 36b8bae7dba3c6e4fde614b6df70caa4  (rules 3513)
   16 entries: f1, f2, f5 + 3.1.5 e186-e197 (3 f-forms + 12 F_-domain)
   + atom (integrand x, atomic top).

   Noise note: the 4,495 `expt: undefined: 0 to a negative exponent.`
   lines (and the scattered `part: argument must be a non-atomic
   expression` lines) are PRE-EXISTING latent-rule noise, not the
   pass-4 mechanism — measured 2026-08-30: only pass 3's lifted
   (mexpt f 1) rescan emits them (passes 1-2 and every direct rule
   evaluation are clean); per-rule isolation on the lifted integrand
   names 1_1_2_1_r33, 1_1_3_1_r66-r70, 1_1_3_4_r80-r81, 2_3_r62,
   2_3_r97-r98, 3_4_r38-r39, the remainder full-table-scan
   context-dependent; no rule was changed (follow-up record:
   .superpowers/sdd/task-1-report.md, Fix report round 1).

   "fired on" attribution (measured in the Task-2 review): the verbose
   print sits in %mr_dispatch AFTER the rule body ran, so a firing
   rule's NESTED sub-integral fires print BEFORE the rule's own line.
   A scan's top-level fire = the LAST "fired on <full integrand>" line
   between its P4SCAN marker and the next; production's = the last
   such line before the PROD line. (An earlier draft of this header
   said "the first such line after the marker" - wrong: it named
   nested fires.)

   Per-entry sweep firings (dir d, bare-factor index i, top-level
   rule; top-level fires identified per the attribution note):
     f2   : P4FIRE (0,1),(0,2),(1,1),(1,2); (0,1)/(1,2) -> 3_1_5_r27
            (3_1_5), (0,2)/(1,1) -> 3_1_3_r8 (3_1_3)
     e186-e193 : P4FIRE (0,1),(1,3); both -> 3_5_r43  (3_5)
     f1, f5, e194-e197, atom : P4SKIP (no sweep fire; atom: atomic
            top, census [0,false] - the guard regression row)

   Expected-table verification (all rows PASS under the 36b8bae7...
   rebuild; a miss would be a mechanism failure):
     f2   : PROD non-noun; census 2,false; sweep>=1 P4FIRE, 3_1_5
            family; production first 3_1_5 fire = 3_1_5_r27 (UNCHANGED
            by the shadow edit - the nil arm is verbatim; global check:
            743/0).
     f1   : PROD noun; census 2,true; P4SKIP; P4DIAG pick-fwd=pick-rev=x^3.
     f5   : PROD noun; census 0,false (mquot top); P4SKIP; no P4DIAG.
     e186-e193 (m=1) : PROD non-noun; census 3,false; sweep>=1 P4FIRE,
            3_5 family; production first 3_5 fire = 3_5_r43.
     e194-e197 (m=2) : PROD noun; census 2,true; P4SKIP; P4DIAG
            pick-fwd=pick-rev=F(a*x)^2.
     atom : NO CRASH (pre-guard: hard error `part: argument must be a
            non-atomic expression` on op(x) - the fix-1 regression);
            PROD non-noun (1_1_1_1_r2 fires on the degenerate x^1 bind
            - the row's purpose is the census line, not the PROD op);
            census 0,false; P4SKIP; no P4DIAG.

   P4* -> label mapping (the Task-2 probe's label vocabulary,
   06-class3-deferred-mechanisms.py label_entry(); recorded so the
   adjudication does not guess it; the plan's PROD-OK is the probe's
   RECORD-MISMATCH):
     a non-noun P4FIRE present                          => FIRE4
     P4SKIP + census (k, true)  (explicit power factor) => 0FIRE-EXPL
     P4SKIP + census (0, false) (non-product top)       => 0FIRE-POOL (nonproduct)
     P4SKIP + census (k>=2, false)                      => 0FIRE-POOL
     production fired + noun PROD                       => D-NEST
     production non-noun PROD (the record said deferred)=> RECORD-MISMATCH
     no DONE line (subprocess died)                     => 0FIRE-POOL (subprocess-died)
 */
batch("probes/corpus/06-calibration.pass4.mac")
cali_entry(name,f,x):=block([ans,census,k,hp,d,i,ans4],
           print(concat("CALI ",name)),rubi_verbose:true,ans:rubi(f,x),
           print(concat("PROD ",
                        if atom(ans) then "atom" else string(op(ans)))),
           census:%mr_barefactors(f),k:part(census,1),hp:part(census,2),
           print(concat("P4CENSUS ",string(k)," ",string(hp))),
           if not atom(f) and is(op(f) = "*")
               then print(concat("P4DIAG ",string(%mr_p4_diag(f)))),
           if is(hp = false) and is(k >= 2)
               then (for d from 0 thru 1 do
                         (for i thru k do
                              (print(concat("P4SCAN ",string(d)," ",
                                            string(i))),
                               ans4:%mr_p4_once(f,x,mr_rule_table,1,d,i),
                               if is(ans4 # false)
                                   then print(
                                   concat("P4FIRE ",string(d)," ",string(i),
                                          " ",
                                          if atom(ans4) then "atom"
                                              else string(op(ans4)))))))
               else print(concat("P4SKIP")),rubi_verbose:false,
           print(concat("CALIEND ",name)))
cali_entry("f2",(d+e*x)*(a+b*log(c*x^n)),x)
